{"title":"Split Array Into K Parts at Minimum Cost","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given an array `a` of `n` integers and an integer `K`. Divide the array into exactly `K` non-empty **contiguous** subarrays (every element belongs to exactly one subarray).\n\nThe cost of a subarray with first element `L` and last element `R` is\n\n`(maximum of the subarray - minimum of the subarray) + |L - R|`.\n\nThe cost of a division is the sum of the costs of its `K` subarrays. Print the minimum possible cost over all divisions.","inputFormat":"The first line contains two integers `n` and `K`.\nThe second line contains `n` integers `a[0], ..., a[n - 1]`.","outputFormat":"Print one integer: the minimum total cost.","constraints":["1 ≤ K ≤ n ≤ 300","-10^9 ≤ a[i] ≤ 10^9"],"examples":[{"input":"4 2\n1 5 2 8","output":"5","explanation":"Split into [1, 5, 2] and [8]. The first part costs (5 - 1) + |1 - 2| = 5, and a single element costs 0. The other splits are worse: [1] | [5, 2, 8] costs 0 + (6 + 3) = 9 and [1, 5] | [2, 8] costs 8 + 12 = 20."},{"input":"3 3\n3 1 4","output":"0","explanation":"K equals n, so every element is its own subarray, and a single-element subarray costs 0."},{"input":"4 1\n4 -2 6 3","output":"9","explanation":"K = 1 forces the whole array as one subarray: (6 - (-2)) + |4 - 3| = 8 + 1 = 9."}],"tests":[{"input":"1 1\n7","output":"0"},{"input":"4 2\n5 5 5 5","output":"0"},{"input":"4 2\n-1000000000 1000000000 -1000000000 1000000000","output":"2000000000"},{"input":"2 1\n-1000000000 1000000000","output":"4000000000"},{"input":"6 3\n1 2 3 4 5 6","output":"6"},{"input":"2 1\n10 0","output":"20"},{"input":"2 2\n-9 10","output":"0"},{"input":"2 2\n-2 -3","output":"0"},{"input":"3 2\n-48 -84 -37","output":"72"},{"input":"3 3\n1 -2 2","output":"0"},{"input":"3 1\n-46 -61 -88","output":"84"},{"input":"4 4\n-3 2 2 -1","output":"0"},{"input":"4 3\n-2 -4 4 -8","output":"4"},{"input":"4 1\n-3 2 1 1","output":"9"},{"input":"5 2\n-48 17 -45 19 -18","output":"99"},{"